  The sum: 5,000,000,000 (treasury) + 993,191,600,000 (bob) + 1,808,400,000 (network fee) = 1,000,000,000,000, the one
  output alice locked and the sweep's one input. Two outputs and no third: nothing is left at the joint address.
  Bob's state: sweep.fee 5000000000, sweep.treasury 49gDG5A6...isG3StWYkFK, sweep.txs [51d1c355...]. Alice's: claimed,
  no sweep, no fee.
  Both processes exited 0: bob "swept the XMR to 42mXZV4k..., less the 5000000000 piconero swap fee paid to the treasury
  49gDG5A6... in the same transaction"; alice "claimed the DERO: tx e2ee6b1c..., stable (stable height 6730)".

Both runs were made before xmr-fee was rebased onto main (which by then carried the zecTreasury and xmrTreasury record
fields and tools/treasurybot). The rebase changed only the record plumbing (netcfg and deploy/networks.json take main's
fields; the simulator's xmrTreasury is the regtest treasury above, as in these runs) and no code the runs executed.

A fault of the driver's, said plainly: an earlier attempt at a separate Refund run found the binary gone (Defender) and its
driver script then stopped on an unset variable, leaving its regtest miner loop running from 16:33 to 19:22. That loop
mined one regtest block about every 6 s to the stage-1 wallet s1cli-1789225277-bob on the shared regtest chain,
including during another run's two minutes under the xmrreg lock. It carried no transaction and moved no coin; it was
stopped when found, and the script's miner now clears its own stop file and its evidence step no longer fails on an
empty id.
